   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three distances",
     "texto": [
      "Japanese distinguishes three distances, unlike English, which has only two: «this» and «that». **これ** = this (near me). **それ** = that (near you). **あれ** = that over there (far from both of us).",
      "These three words stand **alone**. When they go in front of a noun, they change to **この**, **その**, **あの**: **この ほん** (this book), **あの ひと** (that person)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "This, that and that one over there",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Alone",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "In front of a noun",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "near me",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "これ",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "この ほん",
